  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the man as a representative of the stereotype",
  "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto any deictic pronoun like 'me' or 'you' in the text. However, the meme's structure implies that the user is projecting themselves onto the man as the embodiment of the derogatory stereotype 'genuine dumbass mexican'. The user sees the man and interprets him as an instance of that stereotype, thereby projecting their own perspective onto the visual material. The projection is onto the VisualMaterial entity 'man' (the central subject), which is visually anchored by the sombrero and the text overlay. The user is not directly addressed by deictic pronouns, but the meme's intent creates an implicit projection where the viewer identifies the man as the target of the stereotype, making the user a participant in the hateful framing.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
